{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Range"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.pairing_of_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.pairing_of_generator","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**Part (a) of `thm:qou-obstruction-reduction`, conditional on the axiom.**\nLet `pair : H →ₗ[k] k` be integration over the base and suppose\n`pair euler = χ` (Poincaré–Hopf: `χ = 2 − 2g`, supplied as a hypothesis).\nThen a generator of the obstruction line pairs to `χ`, and every obstruction\nclass pairs to a multiple of `χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.eq_smul_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.eq_smul_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L103-L108","doc":"Under (W1) every obstruction class is a scalar multiple of any non-zero one:\nthe obstruction is \"a single scalar\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.exists_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.exists_generator","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L92-L101","doc":"Under the axiom there is a non-zero obstruction class `w` whose archimedean\nimage is the Euler class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.euler_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.euler_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L85-L85","doc":"(W2b) and it is not zero — the base curve is not a torus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.euler_mem_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.euler_mem_range","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L83-L83","doc":"(W2a) the Euler class of the base is realised by an obstruction class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.finrank_obs_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.finrank_obs_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L81-L81","doc":"(W1) the classical-limit obstruction space is a line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WignerAxiom","kind":"class","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/WignerAxiom.lean#L66-L85","doc":"**The Wigner axiom** (`conj:wigner-axiom`).  `Obs` is the classical-limit\nobstruction space (`HH²(𝒰_q, Ad)` of `def:classical-limit-obstruction`) as a\n`k`-vector space, `H` is the archimedean receiving space (`H²(M₀; k)` for the\nbase curve), `realise` is the tower comparison map and `euler` is the Euler\nclass of the tangent bundle of the base.\n\n(W1) the obstruction space is one-dimensional; (W2) the Euler class is a\nnon-zero element of the image of `realise`.  No instance is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:wigner-axiom","label":"conj:wigner-axiom","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/wigner-axiom.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}